 by channel: ATM cash withdrawals, mobile-app-based payments and internet/netbanking payments. Channels overlap with the payment systems (a UPI payment is also a mobile payment), so they must not be added to the system totals."},{"question":"How should I read it?","answer":"ATM withdrawal value growth is a rough guide to cash demand; its slow growth against digital growth shows the shift away from cash."},{"question":"Caveats?","answer":"Channel rows overlap with the payment-system rows. RBI data are provisional and are revised in later releases; the dashboard keeps the latest revision seen. Counts are transactions processed by the system, not unique users or goods purchased."}],"related":[],"layer":"added","note":"Source: RBI monthly Payment System Indicators (provisional, revised in later releases). Volume is in lakh (1 lakh = 100,000 = 0.1 million) transactions; value in Rs. crore (1 crore = 10 million). Published roughly a month after the reference month; history on the RBI site starts June 2021.","scraped_at":"2026-10-30T07:24:28+00:00"}